    {
      "questionId": "q0",
      "value": "q0_pay_when_roi_clear",
      "rationale": "As a busy parent juggling multiple responsibilities, I'd want to validate that FocusLoop actually reduces my stress and saves time before committing money. The free tier lets me test whether it truly consolidates our scattered channels better than what we're doing now.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q1",
      "value": "q1_plus_after_sustained_use",
      "rationale": "Email parsing and shared grocery list sound valuable, but I need to confirm Plus alone handles our family's core needs first. Pro's extra features might be overkill until I'm confident in the base product's daily utility.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q2",
      "value": "q2_monthly_cancel_anytime",
      "rationale": "I prefer flexibility as a busy professional. Monthly lets me exit quickly if priorities shift or if a competing tool emerges. Prepaying annual feels risky when I'm still evaluating whether this fits our workflow long-term.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q3",
      "value": "q3_one_dollar_try_cancel",
      "rationale": "A $1 promo is low-friction enough to test Plus features without guilt. I'd use it to see if digest and task handoffs genuinely simplify our household coordination. If they don't clearly add value, I'll revert to free or stop using it.",
      "confidence": 0.87
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q4",
      "value": "q4_compare_pay_if_wins",
      "rationale": "I'm pragmatic about tools. I'll look at what my friend recommends and compare it fairly against alternatives, including free ones. If FocusLoop genuinely solves our calendar fragmentation better than competitors, I'd pay. Otherwise, I'd stick with what we have.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "value": "q5_ads_pay_if_plus_useful",
      "rationale": "Ads themselves aren't a dealbreaker, but if Plus delivers real family coordination value—like the digest and handoffs—then removing ads becomes a nice bonus, not the main reason to upgrade.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q6",
      "value": "q6_fair_if_use_justifies",
      "rationale": "At $6.99/month Plus and $11.99/month Pro, the pricing is reasonable for a family productivity tool, but only if daily use proves it saves real time and stress. Without that proof, it feels like another subscription to manage.",
      "confidence": 0.89
    },
    {
